  "summary": "pylever exfiltrates Discord tokens found in workspace to hardcoded attacker webhook",
  "details": "The package scans the caller's workspace recursively via rglob('*'), reads every non-binary file's text, and matches Discord bot/user token patterns (regex [MN][A-Za-z0-9_-]{71}). Each hit is validated against the Discord API to enrich it with account metadata (username, id, email, verified flag, bot flag), and then POSTed together with the raw token to a hardcoded Discord webhook (discord.com/api/webhooks/1547416857537945601/...). The module is framed as a 'Discord Token Saver' with private-underscore class names (_Client, _TokenFinder, _TokenValidator, _FileStorage) and ships placeholder author metadata (author='Your Name', author_email='your.email@example.com', url pointing at 'yourusername/pylever'). Installing or importing pylever and invoking its documented API results in Discord credentials discovered on the installer's disk being delivered to a third-party-controlled webhook.",
